ratorname{cosh}⁡(3(t+1)) & -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t+1)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t+1)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t+1))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t+1)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t+1))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-(-1))}\\,x(-1) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t+1)) & -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t+1)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t+1)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t+1))\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t+1)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t+1))\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186391588 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t+1)) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t+1))\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t+1)) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t+1))\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186391589 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t+1)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t+1))\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t+1)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t+1))\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186391590 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t+1)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t+1))\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t+1)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t+1))\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186391591 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t+1)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t+1))\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t+1)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t+1))\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186391592 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t+1)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t+1))\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t+1)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t+1))\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186391682 :question/worked-solution "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨-1,1,1⟩$ and $w=⟨0,2,2⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =2j-2k \\\\  & =⟨0,2,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨0,2,-2⟩.$" "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨-1,1,1⟩$ and $w=⟨0,2,2⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\times \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2j-2k \\\\  & =⟨0,2,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨0,2,-2⟩.$"] [:db/cas 17592186391748 :question/worked-solution "A first-order linear system of differential equations with two dependent variables is a system of equations that takes the following standard form:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=a(t){x}_{1}(t)+b(t){x}_{2}(t)+f(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=c(t){x}_{1}(t)+d(t){x}_{2}(t)+g(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $a(t),$ $b(t),$ $c(t),$ $d(t),$ $f(t),$ and $g(t)$ are known functions, and\n\n- ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are unknown functions (dependent variables).\n\nSuch a system can always be written in the form\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nx(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}a(t) & b(t) \\\\ c(t) & d(t)\\end{aligned}],\\,f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}f(t) \\\\ g(t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe have the following system.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)+7{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)+4{x}_{1}(t)-8{x}_{2}(t)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting our system in standard form, we get the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-7{x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-4{x}_{1}(t)+8{x}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can rewrite our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 8\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "A first-order linear system of differential equations with two dependent variables is a system of equations that takes the following standard form:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=a(t){x}_{1}(t)+b(t){x}_{2}(t)+f(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=c(t){x}_{1}(t)+d(t){x}_{2}(t)+g(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $a(t),$ $b(t),$ $c(t),$ $d(t),$ $f(t),$ and $g(t)$ are known functions, and\n\n- ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are unknown functions (dependent variables).\n\nSuch a system can always be written in the form\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nx(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{bmatrix},\\,A=\\begin{bmatrix}a(t) & b(t) \\\\ c(t) & d(t)\\end{bmatrix},\\,f(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}f(t) \\\\ g(t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWe have the following system.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)+7{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)+4{x}_{1}(t)-8{x}_{2}(t)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting our system in standard form, we get the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-7{x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-4{x}_{1}(t)+8{x}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can rewrite our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 8\\end{bmatrix}x(t)\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 8\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186391750 :answer/value "A=[\\begin{aligned}8 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -7\\end{aligned}]" "A=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -7\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186391751 :answer/value "A=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 8\\end{aligned}]" "A=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 8\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186391752 :answer/value "A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -7 \\\\ -4 & 8\\end{aligned}]" "A=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -7 \\\\ -4 & 8\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186391753 :answer/value "A=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 8\\end{aligned}]" "A=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 8\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186391754 :answer/value "A=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -4\\end{aligned}]" "A=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -4\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186391769 :question/problem "Let $c=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $d=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].$ Find $c+d.$" "Let $c=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}$ and $d=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find $c+d.$"] [:db/cas 17592186391769 :question/worked-solution "We add the vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c+d & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2-3 \\\\ 0+2 \\\\ -1+5 \\\\ 4+7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "We add the vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c+d & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2-3 \\\\ 0+2 \\\\ -1+5 \\\\ 4+7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 11\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186391771 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 11\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186391772 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186391773 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186391774 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 11\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186391775 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186391776 :question/problem "If $b=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]$, then $-\\frac{1}{2}b=$" "If $b=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}$, then $-\\frac{1}{2}b=$"] [:db/cas 17592186391776 :question/worked-solution "Multiplying each component of $b$ by $-\\frac{1}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2}b & =-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2) \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "Multiplying each component of $b$ by $-\\frac{1}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2}b & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2) \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186391778 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186391779 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-16 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-16 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186391780 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186391781 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186391782 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186391783 :question/problem "If $c=[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}]$, then $-\\frac{1}{4}c=$" "If $c=\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 16\\end{bmatrix}$, then $-\\frac{1}{4}c=$"] [:db/cas 17592186391783 :question/worked-solution "Multiplying each component of $c$ by $-\\frac{1}{4},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{4}c & =-\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 12 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (-8) \\\\ -\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 4 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 16\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "Multiplying each component of $c$ by $-\\frac{1}{4},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{4}c & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 16\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 12 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (-8) \\\\ -\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 4 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 16\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186391785 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186391786 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186391787 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186391788 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186391789 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186391790 :question/problem "Find the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}$ given that $3a+2x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -15 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "Find the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}$ given that $3a+2x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}24 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -15 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186391790 :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a+2x & =b \\\\ 2x & =b-3a \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}(b-3a) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}([\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -15 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 14 \\\\ -12 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=6+7=13.$" "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a+2x & =b \\\\ 2x & =b-3a \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}(b-3a) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\begin{bmatrix}24 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -15 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}-3\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ 14 \\\\ -12 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ x & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=6+7=13.$"] [:db/cas 17592186391866 :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" "{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}"] [:db/cas 17592186391868 :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ -3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" "{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ -3{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}"] [:db/cas 17592186391869 :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" "{\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}"] [:db/cas 17592186391870 :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" "{\\begin{bmatrix}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}"] [:db/cas 17592186391871 :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 & 9 \\\\ 4 & 9 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 12\\end{aligned}].$ Find $\\text{Null}(A).$" "Consider the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 6 & 9 \\\\ 4 & 9 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 12\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find $\\text{Null}(A).$"] [:db/cas 17592186391871 :question/worked-solution "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 & 9 \\\\ 4 & 9 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 9 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}-4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, and we have one free variables, ${x}_{3}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ in terms of ${x}_{3}.$\n\nFrom the second equation we get ${x}_{2}=4{x}_{3}.$ Substituting ${x}_{2}=4{x}_{3}$ into the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+2(4{x}_{3})+3{x}_{3}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-11{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nSo the set of all the solutions of $Ax=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={[\\begin{aligned}-11{x}_{3} \\\\ 4{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}.\n$$" "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 6 & 9 \\\\ 4 & 9 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 12\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 9 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 12\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 12\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}-4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, and we have one free variables, ${x}_{3}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ in terms of ${x}_{3}.$\n\nFrom the second equation we get ${x}_{2}=4{x}_{3}.$ Substituting ${x}_{2}=4{x}_{3}$ into the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+2(4{x}_{3})+3{x}_{3}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-11{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nSo the set of all the solutions of $Ax=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={\\begin{bmatrix}-11{x}_{3} \\\\ 4{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186391873 :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{3} \\\\ -11{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}" "{\\begin{bmatrix}4{x}_{3} \\\\ -11{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}"] [:db/cas 17592186391875 :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}-11{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" "{\\begin{bmatrix}-11{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}"] [:db/cas 17592186391876 :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}-11{x}_{3} \\\\ 4{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}" "{\\begin{bmatrix}-11{x}_{3} \\\\ 4{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}"] [:db/cas 17592186391877 :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 4{x}_{1} \\\\ -11{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{1}\\in R}" "{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ 4{x}_{1} \\\\ -11{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}\\,:\\,{x}_{1}\\in R}"] [:db/cas 17592186391903 :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$"] [:db/cas 17592186391903 :question/worked-solution "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ -8 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ -8 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 16\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=10 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=2.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n4{x}_{1}+3\\cdot 2=10\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=1+2=3.$" "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ -8 & 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ -8 & 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 16\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=10 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=2.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n4{x}_{1}+3\\cdot 2=10\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=1+2=3.$"] [:db/cas 17592186391910 :question/problem "Find the vector  $x,$ If  $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}},$ and\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "Find the vector  $x,$ If  $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}},$ and\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186391910 :question/worked-solution "We know that any vector in  $\\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ has the form\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the coordinates relative to the basis $\\,B.$ Since we are told that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={{(\\,-2\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{{(\\,2\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "We know that any vector in  $\\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ has the form\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the coordinates relative to the basis $\\,B.$ Since we are told that $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={{(\\,-2\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+{{(\\,2\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186391912 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186391913 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186391914 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186391915 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -14 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -14 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186391916 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186391917 :question/problem "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.25 & 0.85 \\\\ 0.75 & 0.15\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}0.4 \\\\ 0.6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \nConsider a Markov chain with the stochastic matrix $P$ and the initial state vector ${x}_{0}$ given above. Calculate the state vector ${x}_{2}.$" "$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0.25 & 0.85 \\\\ 0.75 & 0.15\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{0}=\\begin{bmatrix}0.4 \\\\ 0.6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n \nConsider a Markov chain with the stochastic matrix $P$ and the initial state vector ${x}_{0}$ given above. Calculate the state vector ${x}_{2}.$"] [:db/cas 17592186391917 :question/worked-solution "To find the state vector ${x}_{2},$ we apply two steps of the Markov chain:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=P{x}_{0},\\,{x}_{2}=P{x}_{1}\n$$\n\nAfter the first step, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =P{x}_{0} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0.25 & 0.85 \\\\ 0.75 & 0.15\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0.4 \\\\ 0.6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0.61 \\\\ 0.39\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, after the second step, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =P{x}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0.25 & 0.85 \\\\ 0.75 & 0.15\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0.61 \\\\ 0.39\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0.484 \\\\ 0.516\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "To find the state vector ${x}_{2},$ we apply two steps of the Markov chain:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=P{x}_{0},\\,{x}_{2}=P{x}_{1}\n$$\n\nAfter the first step, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =P{x}_{0} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.25 & 0.85 \\\\ 0.75 & 0.15\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0.4 \\\\ 0.6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.61 \\\\ 0.39\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, after the second step, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =P{x}_{1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.25 & 0.85 \\\\ 0.75 & 0.15\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0.61 \\\\ 0.39\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0.484 \\\\ 0.516\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186391919 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0.61 \\\\ 0.39\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}0.61 \\\\ 0.39\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186391920 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0.516 \\\\ 0.484\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}0.516 \\\\ 0.484\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186391921 :answe