$B$ and standard basis $S$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/db/dbd020362f950fe8bfb4c592652b9e78a73610fa01a247b0b7ead6f201bf9ea5.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{S}={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1},\n$$\n\nand the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to S}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -4\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-4)\\cdot 4-3\\cdot (-5)}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the standard basis $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{S} & ={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}11 & 8 \\\\ -10 & -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the basis $B$ and standard basis $S$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/db/dbd020362f950fe8bfb4c592652b9e78a73610fa01a247b0b7ead6f201bf9ea5.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{S}={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1},\n$$\n\nand the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to S}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} & ={\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -4\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-4)\\cdot 4-3\\cdot (-5)}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -3 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the standard basis $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{S} & ={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}11 & 8 \\\\ -10 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186392200 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -6 & -3\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ -6 & -3\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392201 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392202 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 & 5 \\\\ -8 & -7\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 5 \\\\ -8 & -7\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392203 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}11 & 8 \\\\ -10 & -7\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}11 & 8 \\\\ -10 & -7\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392204 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 11 \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 11 \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392205 :question/problem "$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ (shown above) and a basis $C$ of ${R}^{3}.$\nThe matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3}$ relative to these bases, and the vector $x\\in {R}^{2},$ are also given. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$" "$$\nB=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\},\\,[T]_{B|C}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ (shown above) and a basis $C$ of ${R}^{3}.$\nThe matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3}$ relative to these bases, and the vector $x\\in {R}^{2},$ are also given. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$"] [:db/cas 17592186392205 :question/worked-solution "We can find the coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find $[x]_{B},$ the coordinates of $x$ relative to $B.$ So, let\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives us the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-5 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now row-reduce the corresponding augmented matrix using Gaussian elimination, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 10\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 10\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -10 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "We can find the coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find $[x]_{B},$ the coordinates of $x$ relative to $B.$ So, let\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}={x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThis gives us the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-5 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now row-reduce the corresponding augmented matrix using Gaussian elimination, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 10\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 10\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -10 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186392207 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392208 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -10 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -10 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392209 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392210 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392211 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392213 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392214 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 2 & -5\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 2 & -5\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392215 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392216 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 2 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 2 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392217 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392218 :question/problem "Given the matrix\n$\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 10 & -5\\end{aligned}]$\nand $f(x)={x}^{23}-25{x}^{21}-4x+2$, find $f(A).$" "Given the matrix\n$\\,A=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ 10 & -5\\end{bmatrix}$\nand $f(x)={x}^{23}-25{x}^{21}-4x+2$, find $f(A).$"] [:db/cas 17592186392218 :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the characteristic polynomial $p(\\lambda ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & =\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 10 & -5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(5-\\lambda )(-5-\\lambda ) \\\\  & ={\\lambda }^{2}-25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's divide $f(x)$ by $p(x)$ using long division:\n\n|  | $\\,\\,{x}^{21}$ |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}^{2}-25\\,$ | $\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{{x}^{23}\\,-\\,25{x}^{21}\\,-\\,4x\\,+\\,2}$ |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | ${x}^{23}$ | $-$ | $25{x}^{21}$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  |  |  | $-$ | $4x$ | $+$ | $2$ |\n\nTherefore, we can write $f(x)$ as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =q(x)p(x)+r(x) \\\\  & =q(x)p(x)+(-4x+2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $q(x)={x}^{21}.$ Replacing $x$ with $A,$ we have\n\n$$\nf(A)=q(A)p(A)+(-4A+2I).\n$$\n\nAccording to the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have $p(A)=O.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(A) & =q(A)p(A)+(-4A+2I) \\\\  & =q(A)\\cdot O+(-4A+2I) \\\\  & =-4A+2I \\\\  & =-4[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 10 & -5\\end{aligned}]+2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-20 & 0 \\\\ -40 & 20\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-18 & 0 \\\\ -40 & 22\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "Let's start by finding the characteristic polynomial $p(\\lambda ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & =\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I) \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}5-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 10 & -5-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(5-\\lambda )(-5-\\lambda ) \\\\  & ={\\lambda }^{2}-25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's divide $f(x)$ by $p(x)$ using long division:\n\n|  | $\\,\\,{x}^{21}$ |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}^{2}-25\\,$ | $\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{{x}^{23}\\,-\\,25{x}^{21}\\,-\\,4x\\,+\\,2}$ |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | ${x}^{23}$ | $-$ | $25{x}^{21}$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  |  |  | $-$ | $4x$ | $+$ | $2$ |\n\nTherefore, we can write $f(x)$ as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =q(x)p(x)+r(x) \\\\  & =q(x)p(x)+(-4x+2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $q(x)={x}^{21}.$ Replacing $x$ with $A,$ we have\n\n$$\nf(A)=q(A)p(A)+(-4A+2I).\n$$\n\nAccording to the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have $p(A)=O.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(A) & =q(A)p(A)+(-4A+2I) \\\\  & =q(A)\\cdot O+(-4A+2I) \\\\  & =-4A+2I \\\\  & =-4\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ 10 & -5\\end{bmatrix}+2\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-20 & 0 \\\\ -40 & 20\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-18 & 0 \\\\ -40 & 22\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186392220 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 40 \\\\ 0 & -10\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 40 \\\\ 0 & -10\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392221 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-20 & 22 \\\\ -42 & 20\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-20 & 22 \\\\ -42 & 20\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392222 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}18 & 0 \\\\ 40 & -22\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}18 & 0 \\\\ 40 & -22\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392223 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-20 & 40 \\\\ 0 & 20\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-20 & 40 \\\\ 0 & 20\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392224 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-18 & 0 \\\\ -40 & 22\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-18 & 0 \\\\ -40 & 22\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392225 :question/problem "Given the matrix\n$\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 11 \\\\ -3 & -6\\end{aligned}]$\nand $f(x)={x}^{15}-3{x}^{13}+{x}^{3}-5x+6$, find $f(A).$" "Given the matrix\n$\\,A=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 11 \\\\ -3 & -6\\end{bmatrix}$\nand $f(x)={x}^{15}-3{x}^{13}+{x}^{3}-5x+6$, find $f(A).$"] [:db/cas 17592186392225 :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the characteristic polynomial $p(\\lambda )$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & =\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}6-\\lambda  & 11 \\\\ -3 & -6-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(6-\\lambda )(-6-\\lambda )+33 \\\\  & ={\\lambda }^{2}-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's divide $f(x)$ by $p(x)$ using long division:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"left\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\,{x}^{13}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$+$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{2}-3\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"7\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{{x}^{15}-3{x}^{13}+{x}^{3}-5x+6\\phantom{|}}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{15}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\,\\,\\,-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\,\\,\\,3{x}^{13}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{3}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\,5x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,+$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{3}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\,3x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\,2x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,+$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nTherefore, we can write $f(x)$ as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =q(x)p(x)+r(x) \\\\  & =q(x)p(x)+(-2x+6)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $q(x)={x}^{13}+x.$ Replacing $x$ with $A,$ we have\n\n$$\nf(A)=q(A)p(A)+(-2A+6I).\n$$\n\nAccording to the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have $p(A)=O.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(A) & =q(A)p(A)+(-2A+6I) \\\\  & =q(A)\\cdot O+(-2A+6I) \\\\  & =-2A+6I \\\\  & =-2[\\begin{aligned}6 & 11 \\\\ -3 & -6\\end{aligned}]+6[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-12 & -22 \\\\ 6 & 12\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -22 \\\\ 6 & 18\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "Let's start by finding the characteristic polynomial $p(\\lambda )$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & =\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I) \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}6-\\lambda  & 11 \\\\ -3 & -6-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(6-\\lambda )(-6-\\lambda )+33 \\\\  & ={\\lambda }^{2}-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's divide $f(x)$ by $p(x)$ using long division:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"left\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\,{x}^{13}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$+$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{2}-3\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"7\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{{x}^{15}-3{x}^{13}+{x}^{3}-5x+6\\phantom{|}}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{15}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\,\\,\\,-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\,\\,\\,3{x}^{13}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{3}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\,5x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,+$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{3}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\,3x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=