in{aligned}-22 & -6 \\\\ 6 & 18\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-22 & -6 \\\\ 6 & 18\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392233 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-25 & -14 \\\\ 16 & 9\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-25 & -14 \\\\ 16 & 9\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392234 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & -18 \\\\ 2 & -7\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -18 \\\\ 2 & -7\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392235 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392236 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & -10 \\\\ -4 & 13\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -10 \\\\ -4 & 13\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392237 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}11 & 6 \\\\ -20 & -11\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}11 & 6 \\\\ -20 & -11\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392238 :question/problem "$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -4\\end{aligned}],\\,[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSuppose $B$ and $C$ are bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W,$ respectively. The matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:V\\to W$ relative to these bases, and the coordinates of the vector $x\\in V$ relative to $B$ are shown above. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$" "$$\n[T]_{B|C}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -1 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -4\\end{bmatrix},\\,[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSuppose $B$ and $C$ are bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W,$ respectively. The matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:V\\to W$ relative to these bases, and the coordinates of the vector $x\\in V$ relative to $B$ are shown above. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$"] [:db/cas 17592186392238 :question/worked-solution "The coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-22 \\\\ 26\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "The coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -1 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-22 \\\\ 26\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186392240 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-26 \\\\ 22\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-26 \\\\ 22\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392241 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-22 \\\\ 26\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-22 \\\\ 26\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392242 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392243 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 16\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392244 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392245 :question/worked-solution "Since we have $\\,T({b}_{1})={b}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,T({b}_{2})=2{b}_{1}\\,$, we have\n\n$$\n[T({b}_{1})]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the $B$-matrix for $T$ is a matrix  whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $B.$ Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n[\\,T\\,]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "Since we have $\\,T({b}_{1})={b}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,T({b}_{2})=2{b}_{1}\\,$, we have\n\n$$\n[T({b}_{1})]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, the $B$-matrix for $T$ is a matrix  whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $B.$ Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n[\\,T\\,]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186392247 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392248 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392249 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392250 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392251 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392252 :question/worked-solution "Since we have $\\,T({b}_{1})={b}_{1}-{b}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,T({b}_{2})=2{b}_{1}-2{b}_{2}\\,$, we have\n\n$$\n[T({b}_{1})]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the $B$-matrix for $T$ is a matrix  whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $B.$ Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n[\\,T\\,]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "Since we have $\\,T({b}_{1})={b}_{1}-{b}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,T({b}_{2})=2{b}_{1}-2{b}_{2}\\,$, we have\n\n$$\n[T({b}_{1})]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, the $B$-matrix for $T$ is a matrix  whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $B.$ Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n[\\,T\\,]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186392254 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392255 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392256 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392257 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392258 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -5\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -5\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392259 :question/problem "If $\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5-\\text{i} \\\\ \\text{i} & -3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1-2\\text{i} & 1+2\\text{i} \\\\ -1 & 2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$, then $AB=$" "If $\\,A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5-\\text{i} \\\\ \\text{i} & -3\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1-2\\text{i} & 1+2\\text{i} \\\\ -1 & 2\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}\\,$, then $AB=$"] [:db/cas 17592186392259 :question/worked-solution "Multiplying the matrices using the usual method, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5-\\text{i} \\\\ \\text{i} & -3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1-2\\text{i} & 1+2\\text{i} \\\\ -1 & 2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(1)(1-2\\text{i})+(5-\\text{i})(-1) & (1)(1+2\\text{i})+(5-\\text{i})(2\\text{i}) \\\\ (\\text{i})(1-2\\text{i})+(-3\\text{i})(-1) & (\\text{i})(1+2\\text{i})+(-3\\text{i})(2\\text{i})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(1-2\\text{i})+(-5+\\text{i}) & (1+2\\text{i})+(2+10\\text{i}) \\\\ (2+\\text{i})+(3\\text{i}) & (-2+\\text{i})+(6)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4-\\text{i} & 3+12\\text{i} \\\\ 2+4\\text{i} & 4+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n." "Multiplying the matrices using the usual method, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5-\\text{i} \\\\ \\text{i} & -3\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1-2\\text{i} & 1+2\\text{i} \\\\ -1 & 2\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}(1)(1-2\\text{i})+(5-\\text{i})(-1) & (1)(1+2\\text{i})+(5-\\text{i})(2\\text{i}) \\\\ (\\text{i})(1-2\\text{i})+(-3\\text{i})(-1) & (\\text{i})(1+2\\text{i})+(-3\\text{i})(2\\text{i})\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}(1-2\\text{i})+(-5+\\text{i}) & (1+2\\text{i})+(2+10\\text{i}) \\\\ (2+\\text{i})+(3\\text{i}) & (-2+\\text{i})+(6)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4-\\text{i} & 3+12\\text{i} \\\\ 2+4\\text{i} & 4+\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n."] [:db/cas 17592186392261 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4-\\text{i} & 3+12\\text{i} \\\\ 2+4\\text{i} & 4+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}4-\\text{i} & 3+12\\text{i} \\\\ 2+4\\text{i} & 4+\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392262 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4-\\text{i} & 3+12\\text{i} \\\\ 2+4\\text{i} & 4+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-4-\\text{i} & 3+12\\text{i} \\\\ 2+4\\text{i} & 4+\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392263 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4+\\text{i} & -3-12\\text{i} \\\\ -2-4\\text{i} & -4-\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}4+\\text{i} & -3-12\\text{i} \\\\ -2-4\\text{i} & -4-\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392264 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4-\\text{i} & 3+12\\text{i} \\\\ 4+2\\text{i} & 1+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-4-\\text{i} & 3+12\\text{i} \\\\ 4+2\\text{i} & 1+\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392265 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\text{i} & 12\\text{i} \\\\ 2+4\\text{i} & 4+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\text{i} & 12\\text{i} \\\\ 2+4\\text{i} & 4+\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392266 :question/problem "$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}\\text{i}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the vector $v$ and the rotation-scaling matrix $C$ shown above. Given that $v$ is an eigenvector of a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-1+2\\text{i},$ find a matrix $P$ such that $A=PC{P}^{-1}.$" "$$\nv=\\begin{bmatrix}\\text{i}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the vector $v$ and the rotation-scaling matrix $C$ shown above. Given that $v$ is an eigenvector of a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-1+2\\text{i},$ find a matrix $P$ such that $A=PC{P}^{-1}.$"] [:db/cas 17592186392266 :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any $2\\times 2$ real matrix $A$ with complex eigenvalues, we have $A=PC{P}^{-1},$ where \n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nand $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to the complex eigenvalue  $\\lambda .$\n\nFirst, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}]=C.\n$$\n\nNext, we can find the real and imaginary parts of our eigenvector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =[\\begin{aligned}\\text{i}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]={{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(v)}+\\text{i}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(v)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now construct $P:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "Recall that for any $2\\times 2$ real matrix $A$ with complex eigenvalues, we have $A=PC{P}^{-1},$ where \n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nand $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to the complex eigenvalue  $\\lambda .$\n\nFirst, notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=C.\n$$\n\nNext, we can find the real and imaginary parts of our eigenvector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\text{i}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}={{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(v)}+\\text{i}{{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(v)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now construct $P:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =\\begin{bmatrix}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186392268 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392269 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392270 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392271 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392272 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392274 :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}" "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}"] [:db/cas 17592186392275 :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}" "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}"] [:db/cas 17592186392276 :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}" "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}"] [:db/cas 17592186392277 :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}" "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}"] [:db/cas 17592186392278 :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}" "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}"] [:db/cas 17592186392280 :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]{2}^{t}" "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}{2}^{t}"] [:db/cas 17592186392281 :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]{2}^{t}" "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}{2}^{t}"] [:db/cas 17592186392282 :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]{2}^{t}" "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}{2}^{t}"] [:db/cas 17592186392283 :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)\\end{aligned}]{2}^{t}" "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)\\end{bmatrix}{2}^{t}"] [:db/cas 17592186392284 :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]{2}^{t}" "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}{2}^{t}"] [:db/cas 17592186392285 :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]x(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{6} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186392285 :question/worked-solution "We have a decoupled system. Therefore, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\sqrt{6}t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial condition $x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to our initial value problem is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\sqrt{6}t}+0\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\sqrt{6}t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "We have a decoupled system. Therefore, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{\\sqrt{6}t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial condition $x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to our initial value problem is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =2\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{\\sqrt{6}t}+0\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{\\sqrt{6}t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186392287 :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\sqrt{6}t}" "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{\\sqrt{6}t}"] [:db/cas 17592186392288 :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\sqrt{6}t}" "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{6} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{\\sqrt{6}t}"] [:db/cas 17592186392289 :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\sqrt{6}t}" "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{\\sqrt{6}t}"] [:db/cas 17592186392290 :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\sqrt{6}t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}" "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{\\sqrt{6}t}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}"] [:db/cas 17592186392291 :answer/value "x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{\\sqrt{6}t}" "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{6} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{\\sqrt{6}t}"] [:db/cas 17592186392299 :question/problem "Let ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ be eigenvectors of a matrix $A.$ Find the decoupling matrix of the differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t).$" "Let ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$ and ${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$ be eigenvectors of a matrix $A.$ Find the decoupling matrix of the differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t).$"] [:db/cas 17592186392299 :question/worked-solution "First, we construct the matrix $E$, whose columns are the eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}:$\n\n$$\nE=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, the decoupling matrix can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={E}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot (-2)}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "First, we construct the matrix $E$, whose columns are the eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}:$\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, the decoupling matrix can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={E}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot (-2)}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186392301 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392302 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392303 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392304 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392305 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392306 :question/problem "Let ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$ and ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ be eigenvectors of a matrix $A.$ Find the decoupling matrix of the differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t).$" "Let ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}$ and ${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ be eigenvectors of a matrix $A.$ Find the decoupling matrix of the differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t).$"] [:db/cas 17592186392306 :question/worked-solution "First, we construct the matrix $E$, whose columns are the eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}:$\n\n$$\nE=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, the decoupling matrix can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={E}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 3-5\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "First, we construct the matrix $E$, whose columns are the eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}:$\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, the decoupling matrix can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={E}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 3-5\\cdot 1}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186392308 :answer/value "D=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}]" "D=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392309 :answer/value "D=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}]" "D=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392310 :answer/value "D=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}]" "D=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392311 :answer/value "D=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" "D=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392312 :answer/value "D=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" "D=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392313 :question/problem "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the orthogonal projection of $a$ onto $\\text{Span}{b}.$" "Let $a=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}$ and $b=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find the orthogonal projection of $a$ onto $\\text{Span}{b}.$"] [:db/cas 17592186392313 :question/worked-solution "The orthogonal projection of $a$ onto $\\text{Span}{b}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{b\\cdot a}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 2+(-3)\\cdot (-3)+1\\cdot 4}{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{4+4+9+4}{16+4+9+1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{21}{30}b \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{10}b \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{10}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{14}{5} \\\\ \\frac{7}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{21}{10} \\\\ \\frac{7}{10}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "The orthogonal projection of $a$ onto $\\text{Span}{b}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{b\\cdot a}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 2+(-3)\\cdot (-3)+1\\cdot 4}{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{4+4+9+4}{16+4+9+1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{21}{30}b \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{10}b \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{10}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{14}{5} \\\\ \\frac{7}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{21}{10} \\\\ \\frac{7}{10}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186392315 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{21}{10} \\\\ \\frac{7}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{21}{10} \\\\ \\frac{14}{5}\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{21}{10} \\\\ \\frac{7}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{21}{10} \\\\ \\frac{14}{5}\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392316 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392317 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392318 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{4} \\\\ \\frac{7}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ \\frac{7}{10}\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{5}{4} \\\\ \\frac{7}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ \\frac{7}{10}\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392319 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{14}{5} \\\\ \\frac{7}{5}