gonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by \n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x+{\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1}\\}$ and $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{2}\\}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot v}{v\\cdot v}v=\\frac{3\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 1}{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}v=\\frac{2}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot w}{w\\cdot w}w=\\frac{3\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 1}{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}w=\\frac{11}{6}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x+{\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{11}{6}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(4[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+11[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "Since our plane passes through the origin, it defines the subspace $S=\\text{Span}\\{v,w\\}$ in ${R}^{3}.$ \nAnd, since the set $\\{v,w\\}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by \n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x+{\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1}\\}$ and $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{2}\\}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot v}{v\\cdot v}v=\\frac{3\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 1}{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}v=\\frac{2}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot w}{w\\cdot w}w=\\frac{3\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 1}{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}w=\\frac{11}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x+{\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\frac{11}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(4\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+11\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186392342 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392343 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392344 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 3 \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 3 \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392345 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ \\frac{5}{4} \\\\ \\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ \\frac{5}{4} \\\\ \\frac{5}{4}\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392346 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2}{5}\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392347 :question/problem "Given the **orthonormal** basis $B={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{26}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}}\\end{aligned}]}$  of ${R}^{2},$ find $[x]_{B}$ if $x=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" "Given the **orthonormal** basis $B={\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{26}}\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}}\\end{bmatrix}}$  of ${R}^{2},$ find $[x]_{B}$ if $x=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$"] [:db/cas 17592186392347 :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${