n vector by computing the displacement vector between the given points $H(5,7,2)$ and $S(3,4,5),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{HS} \\\\  & =⟨3,4,5⟩-⟨5,7,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,-3,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector equation of the line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186392968 :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" "r=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] [:db/cas 17592186392969 :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" "r=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] [:db/cas 17592186392970 :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" "r=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] [:db/cas 17592186392971 :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" "r=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] [:db/cas 17592186392972 :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" "r=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] [:db/cas 17592186392980 :question/problem "Find $Lz$ if \n$L=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$z=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" "Find $Lz$ if \n$L=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$z=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$"] [:db/cas 17592186392980 :question/worked-solution "We multiply each row in the matrix by the column vector using the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Lz & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1\\cdot (-3)+0\\cdot 8+4\\cdot 2 \\\\ 1\\cdot (-3)+3\\cdot 8+(-2)\\cdot 2 \\\\ 2\\cdot (-3)+0\\cdot 8+(-5)\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3+0+8 \\\\ -3+24-4 \\\\ -6+0-10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 17 \\\\ -16\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "We multiply each row in the matrix by the column vector using the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Lz & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1\\cdot (-3)+0\\cdot 8+4\\cdot 2 \\\\ 1\\cdot (-3)+3\\cdot 8+(-2)\\cdot 2 \\\\ 2\\cdot (-3)+0\\cdot 8+(-5)\\cdot 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3+0+8 \\\\ -3+24-4 \\\\ -6+0-10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 17 \\\\ -16\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186392982 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 17 \\\\ -16\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 17 \\\\ -16\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392983 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 17 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 17 \\\\ 16\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392984 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -17 \\\\ -16\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -17 \\\\ -16\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392985 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 17 \\\\ -16\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 17 \\\\ -16\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392986 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -17 \\\\ -16\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -17 \\\\ -16\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186392994 :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(1,-4,5)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(1,-4,5)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$"] [:db/cas 17592186392994 :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the position vector of $P$ is $p=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$ and $n=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ is normal to the plane. \n\nThe equation of the plane that passes though the point $P({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(r-p)\\cdot n=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $p$ is the position vector of $P.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =-11.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "First, notice that the position vector of $P$ is $p=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}$ and $n=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$ is normal to the plane. \n\nThe equation of the plane that passes though the point $P({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(r-p)\\cdot n=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $p$ is the position vector of $P.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\